STORY: Burglar smashes into Miami Beach restaurant, steals cash register drawer, surveillance video shows
ARTICLE CHARS: 2276

HEADLINES:
BURGLAR SMASHES MIAMI BEACH RESTAURANT DOOR AND STEALS CASH REGISTER DRAWER
CASH DRAWER STOLEN IN MIAMI BEACH RESTAURANT BREAK IN
TEN YEAR NORMANDY DRIVE RESTAURANT TARGETED IN EARLY MORNING BREAK IN

ARTICLE:
A burglar smashed through the front glass door of 7tyone Restaurant & Coffee Bar on Normandy Drive in Miami Beach around 1 a.m. Friday, stealing the entire cash register drawer.

Owner Liliana Arguinzones, who moved from Venezuela and has operated the Normandy Isle business for ten years, learned of the crime hours later from a neighboring business. Upon arriving, she discovered heaps of shattered glass and a brick left near the entrance.

Surveillance cameras captured the burglar wearing a hat and using a rag to cover his face before ripping the drawer from the front counter.

Miami Beach Police are investigating the burglary. Tipsters can call Crime Stoppers at 305-471-TIPS.
